WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.484
You read a fictional estate of
thirty-five identities into one register,

3
00:00:05.484 --> 00:00:10.016
found the eight high-risk ones, saw
the reader refuse an undeclared call,

4
00:00:10.016 --> 00:00:15.162
and handed three SQL Server and LDAP-bind
accounts to the Data Platform plan.

5
00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:19.816
The evidence an ISSO keeps for Gate
1 from this module is the register,

6
00:00:19.816 --> 00:00:23.816
the findings, the hand-off and
the manifest that hashes them,

7
00:00:23.816 --> 00:00:28.062
all dated; the permission list from
step two; and the test result.

8
00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:31.137
Before you ship, work through
the chapter's checklist.

9
00:00:31.137 --> 00:00:35.650
Next is Module 2: owners,
sponsors and the orphan rule.

10
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.913
Every identity in this register
needs two human owners and a sponsor,

11
00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:44.450
and Module 2 checks who they are and
what happens when there's nobody left.
